{"name":"Slumber","hex":"#2d517c","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"slumber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very light state of sleep, almost awake.","A state of ignorance or inaction."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be in a very light state of sleep, almost awake.","To be inactive or negligent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slumber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slumber (dog)","blocks":[{"text":"Ch. Slumber was an Old English Sheepdog that won best in show at the Westminster Kennel Club Dog Show in 1914. He was owned by Mrs. Tyler Morse and was \"hands down\" the winner of the show. Slumber's win in 1914 is credited with having promoted the popularity of the breed today."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Slumber_old_english_sheepdog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slumber_(dog)","wikidata":"Q7542293"},{"title":"Slumber (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Slumber is a 2017 British supernatural horror-thriller film directed by Jonathan Hopkins and co-written by Richard Hobley and Hopkins. It stars Maggie Q, Kristen Bush, Sam Troughton, Will Kemp, William Hope and Sylvester McCoy."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2f/Slumber_%28film_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slumber_(film)","wikidata":"Q23707694"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Slumber_old_english_sheepdog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Slumber_old_english_sheepdog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASlumber_old_english_sheepdog.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki